# Sidemantic Development Guidelines

When modifying the sidemantic repository, follow these essential practices:

## 1. Read the README First
- Always consult [README.md](mdc:README.md) before making changes
- Ensure all extra dependencies are installed as specified
- Follow the development setup instructions

## 2. Code Quality Standards
- Respect the existing code style and conventions
- Follow the project's linting and formatting rules
- Maintain consistency with existing patterns

## 3. Testing Requirements
- **Always add or fix corresponding unit tests for your changes**
- Ensure all existing unit tests continue to pass
- Run the full test suite before committing changes
- Write tests that cover both happy path and edge cases

## 4. Development Workflow
- Install dependencies: `uv run pip install -e .`
- Run tests: `uv run python -m pytest tests/`
- Check code style and linting
- Verify functionality with integration tests

## 5. Test Categories
- **Unit Tests**: Test individual functions and methods
- **Integration Tests**: Test component interactions
- **End-to-End Tests**: Test complete workflows

## 6. Commit Standards
- Write clear, descriptive commit messages
- Include test coverage in your commits
- Document any breaking changes

Remember: Always ensure your changes are thoroughly tested and don't break existing functionality.